From: Luis Mita <luis@luismita.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: fix PPE flow accounting double count

mtk_flow_entry_update() folds the per-slot MIB accumulator into the
flow's banked totals (prev_packets/prev_bytes) once the FOE entry is no
longer in BIND state, but it adds the same accumulator to the caller's
snapshot on every call.  mtk_foe_entry_get_stats() re-initialises that
snapshot from the banked totals on each query, so from the second query
after the slot left BIND onwards the reported delta is the entire
lifetime packet/byte count again.

netfilter consumes these deltas with nf_ct_acct_add(), so a sparse
one-way flow whose flowtable entry outlives its PPE slot inflates the
conntrack counters by one full counter value per stats query.  Observed
as ~30x inflation over the ~30s between the slot ageing out and the
flow being torn down:

  ipv4 2 udp 17 ... packets=150000 ...    (BIND)
  ipv4 2 udp 17 ... packets=1049730 ...   (slot gone, +1x)
  ipv4 2 udp 17 ... packets=2549280 ...   (+1x)
  ipv4 2 udp 17 ... packets=4048830 ...   (+1x)
  ipv4 2 udp 17 ... packets=4498695 ...   (+1x, then teardown)

Fold the accumulator into the snapshot exactly once and consume it so
that later queries report no further traffic.  This also stops a FOE
slot that is reused before its next bind from exposing the previous
flow's counters through the debugfs interface.

Fixes: aa2777145f8d ("kernel: improve mtk ppe flow accounting")
Signed-off-by: Luis Mita <luis@luismita.com>
---

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -718,7 +718,6 @@
 	struct mtk_foe_entry foe = {};
 	struct mtk_foe_entry *hwe;
 	u16 hash = entry->hash;
-	bool ret = false;
 	int len;
 
 	if (hash == 0xffff)
@@ -732,24 +731,31 @@
 	    FIELD_GET(MTK_FOE_IB1_STATE, foe.ib1) != MTK_FOE_STATE_BIND) {
 		acct = mtk_ppe_acct_data(ppe, hash);
 		if (acct) {
+			/*
+			 * The slot is no longer bound. Fold its final
+			 * counters into the flow's banked totals and
+			 * consume the accumulator, so that repeated
+			 * stats queries do not account for it again.
+			 */
 			entry->prev_packets += acct->packets;
 			entry->prev_bytes += acct->bytes;
+			*packets += acct->packets;
+			*bytes += acct->bytes;
+			acct->packets = 0;
+			acct->bytes = 0;
 		}
 
-		goto out;
+		return false;
 	}
 
 	entry->data.ib1 = foe.ib1;
 	acct = mtk_ppe_mib_entry_read(ppe, hash);
-	ret = true;
-
-out:
 	if (acct) {
 		*packets += acct->packets;
 		*bytes += acct->bytes;
 	}
 
-	return ret;
+	return true;
 }
 
 static void
